   "subject": "Ordinal data and sampling weights",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Dear all, <div><br></div><div>I was wondering if it is possible to include weights when data are ordinal? </div><div>In the following model, should these be included: </div><div>cfa (specified_model, data = cfa_dataset,  <a href=\"http://std.lv\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414593220000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1ndYBdt0jYwRDv5KlN2aOd\">std.lv</a> = TRUE, meanstructure = T, estimator = &quot;WLSMV&quot;, missing = &quot;pairwise&quot;, ordered = TRUE, sampling.weights = &quot;wgt&quot;) or removed?</div><div><br></div><div>Thank you in advance.</div><div>AAS</div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "T-Ehjsj_AAAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2024-06-11T09:09:24Z",
   "subject": "Re: Ordinal data and sampling weights",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div>I was wondering if it is possible to include weights when data are ordinal? </div><div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><div>Yes, but only when using pairwise ML estimation.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div><div> </div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><font face=\"Courier New\" size=\"2\">cfa (specified_model, data = cfa_dataset,  <a href=\"http://std.lv\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://std.lv&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414593221000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2uN2dk1VO32rXncoxfBp7P\">std.lv</a> = TRUE, meanstructure = T, </font></div></blockquote></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><blockquote style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div> <font face=\"Courier New\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"background-color:white\">     </span><span style=\"background-color:yellow\">estimator = &quot;PML&quot;</span>, missing = &quot;pairwise&quot;, ordered = TRUE, sampling.weights = &quot;wgt&quot;) </font></div></blockquote><div> </div><div>Of course, PML also makes better <font face=\"Courier New\">missing= </font>options available:</div><div><a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111/bmsp.12243\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://doi.org/10.1111/bmsp.12243&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792414593221000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2IIhfZ4VIFUiZtBnm9GQIT\">https://doi.org/10.1111/bmsp.12243</a><br></div><div>(see syntax examples in Appendix E of their supplemental file)</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"color:rgb(33,33,33);font-family:Aptos;font-size:16px\"><div><p style=\"margin:0cm;line-height:normal;font-size:11pt;font-family:Calibri,sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\">Terrence D. Jorgensen </span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\">   (he, him, his)</span><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:1.2\"><br>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics<br>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam<br><a href=\"https://eur04.safelinks.protection.outlook.com/?url=https%3A%2F%2Furldefense.com%2Fv3%2F__http%3A%2Fwww.uva.nl%2Fprofile%2Ft.d.jorgensen__%3B!!D9dNQwwGXtA!RdmdUd4WPRh7g7WAPQViCxUMWWjfCFpYPBs_GolbBQ-8m6MZFr9q93hgVEl4SnZ0IqPtX17qKMdVIrknwgORIVJK-9w%24&amp;data=05%...%40uva.nl%7C787cddbcbb304d36cd2808dc896574a6%7Ca0f1cacd618c4403b94576fb3d6874e5%7C0%7C0%7C638536316050859803%7CUnknown%7CTWFpbGZsb3d8eyJWIjoiMC4wLjAwMDAiLCJQIjoiV2luMzIiLCJBTiI6Ik1haWwiLCJXVCI6Mn0%3D%7C0%7C%7C%7C&amp;sdata=m0lXbiRM61LU8SlXmHCEAbZGCI%2F39ZSVK%2FOV6SuCMpY%3D&amp;reserved=0\" titl